ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:76cca60d   none  introduces the list
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:221d4f1a  none  the precedence of the internationalization variables is stated once, in XBD 8.2, and asserted there (XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.001 to .004); no locale category this utility consults has a standard-defined, observable effect that a made locale could show
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:8aece102  none  the precedence of the internationalization variables is stated once, in XBD 8.2, and asserted there (XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.001 to .004); no locale category this utility consults has a standard-defined, observable effect that a made locale could show
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:b96c5038  none  the precedence of the internationalization variables is stated once, in XBD 8.2, and asserted there (XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.001 to .004); no locale category this utility consults has a standard-defined, observable effect that a made locale could show
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:4a460d8d  untestable  the utility handles its operands and data as names, numbers, keywords or opaque bytes; how bytes group into characters changes nothing the page specifies, so no observable difference can be required
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:fb479014  untestable  the wording and layout of diagnostic messages are unspecified (the page says only that they should follow the locale), so no locale-dependent result can be required
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:c3667fa1  impl  outside the POSIX locale the format and contents of the date and time strings are not specified by the page
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:d838b9f5  impl  the format of message catalogs and the messages a utility looks up in them are implementation-defined, so a catalog search cannot be observed in a portable way
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:6eb2b4f1  untestable  login records are kept by the system and a test cannot create one
ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES:bdf7eb3f  impl  the default time zone is unspecified
